{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CexGw2oWwgzmexRRwSqUc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011Y5ZWfvAjNan51P3wABDEq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement the confirm shipment endpoint","prompt":"You are helping implement the BE-003 task for a Kotlin + Spring Boot shipment API. \n\nYour task is to:\n\n1. Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION` to the ErrorCode enum in `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt`. The enum currently has: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED. Add the new code after SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS.\n\n2. Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` to the ShipmentController in `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt`. The endpoint should:\n   - Accept a shipmentId path parameter\n   - Find the shipment by ID, throwing ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If the shipment status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED\n   - If the shipment status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - If the shipment status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION error code and message \"Cannot confirm a shipment in CANCELLED status\"\n   - Return the updated shipment\n   - Use ResponseEntity.ok() for the response\n\n3. Add tests to ShipmentControllerTest in `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` for:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment changes its status to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and makes no change\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns HTTP 409 with error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns HTTP 404\n\nBe careful to preserve the existing code and tests - only add what is necessary. Use POST request builders in the tests like the existing create test does."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":33485,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":350},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24402fd9-b714-4b41-86f7-6f1d1b0b434b","uuid":"60d52d6a-2ad6-4b20-8a5d-0907b917535c","timestamp":"2026-09-11T20:22:40.256Z","request_id":"req_011CexGw2EXY9j8TwdiY9FPc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011Y5ZWfvAjNan51P3wABDEq":{"description":"Implement the confirm shipment endpoint","prompt":"You are helping implement the BE-003 task for a Kotlin + Spring Boot shipment API. \n\nYour task is to:\n\n1. Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION` to the ErrorCode enum in `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt`. The enum currently has: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED. Add the new code after SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS.\n\n2. Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` to the ShipmentController in `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt`. The endpoint should:\n   - Accept a shipmentId path parameter\n   - Find the shipment by ID, throwing ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If the shipment status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED\n   - If the shipment status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n   - If the shipment status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION error code and message \"Cannot confirm a shipment in CANCELLED status\"\n   - Return the updated shipment\n   - Use ResponseEntity.ok() for the response\n\n3. Add tests to ShipmentControllerTest in `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` for:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment changes its status to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and makes no change\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns HTTP 409 with error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns HTTP 404\n\nBe careful to preserve the existing code and tests - only add what is necessary. Use POST request builders in the tests like the existing create test does."}}}
