{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mi4QQbSj3xXguRjUBTL7nG","type":"tool_result","content":"jirihermann      46785   1.7  0.5 440879168 347104   ??  SN   10:21PM   0:02.76 claude --permission-mode acceptEdits --strict-mcp-config --allowedTools Bash(./mvnw:*) Bash(mvn:*) --disable-slash-commands --setting-sources project --model claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 --output-format stream-json --verbose -p # BE-003 — Confirm shipment\\012\\012## Requirement\\012\\012A shipment is created in `CREATED` status and there is currently no way to move it on.\\012Operations need to confirm a shipment once the carrier has accepted it.\\012\\012Add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`.\\012\\012- Confirming a shipment that is `CREATED` moves it to `CONFIRMED` and returns the shipment.\\012- **Confirming a shipment that is already `CONFIRMED` succeeds and changes nothing.**\\012  Operations retries this call, and a retry must not fail.\\012- Confirming a shipment that is `CANCELLED` is rejected with HTTP 409.\\012- Confirming a shipment that does not exist is rejected with HTTP 404.\\012\\012## Constraints\\012\\012- The existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture must be preserved.\\012- Do not add new dependencies.\\012- Do not modify files outside the shipment feature, except tests if required.\\012\\012## Acceptance criteria\\012\\0121. Existing build passes.\\0122. Existing tests pass.\\0123. `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it.\\0124. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\\0125. A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused.\\0126. No new Maven dependency appears.\\0127. No unrelated production file changes.\\012\\012## Notes for the agent\\012\\012The service under test is `sample-service`. Run `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` to\\012verify your work before finishing.\njirihermann      78741   1.6  0.2 509064528 166960 s016  S+   13J