shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it.\\0124. Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API.\\0125. A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused.\\0126. No new Maven dependency appears.\\0127. No unrelated production file changes.\\012\\012## Notes for the agent\\012\\012The service under test is `sample-service`. Run `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` to\\012verify your work before finishing.\njirihermann      78741   1.6  0.2 509064528 166960 s016  S+   13Jul26 302:12.95 claude --dangerously-skip-permissions You are delivering tool 17-skills-registry of the UnityInFlow ecosystem, in its own git repo.\\012The business case and feature spec for this tool is 17-skills-registry.md in this directory — it is the source of truth for scope (problem statement, v0.1 feature checklist, stack, implementation todos). CLAUDE.md carries the acceptance criteria and ecosystem constraints.\\0121. Read CLAUDE.md and 17-skills-registry.md fully before anything else.\\0122. Invoke the gsd-ingest-docs skill to bootstrap the .planning/ setup from 17-skills-registry.md and CLAUDE.md, so the business case becomes the GSD project's requirements and roadmap. If ingest leaves gaps, fill them with gsd-new-project using the spec's content — do not invent scope beyond the spec.\\0123. Then invoke gsd-autonomous to run all phases (discuss -> plan -> execute -> verify per phase) until the v0.0.1 acceptance criteria in CLAUDE.md are met.\\0124. Follow the ecosystem constraints (stack, ktlint/clippy/ruff, test coverage >80% on core logic, no secrets, atomic commits per task).\\0125. Whenever a decision needs the user, record it in .planning/OPEN-QUESTIONS.md, choose the most conservative option, and continue — do not stall waiting for input.\\0126. Stop at the release step: prepare everything for v0.0.1 (build green, tests passing, README/CONTRIBUTING/LICENSE/ci.yml present) but do NOT publish to npm/Maven Central/cra