{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CexJuj8LUCCYyA8K6xAdc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M9enFxs4TE13FnLgxT3LDp","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Add confirm endpoint tests to ShipmentControllerTest","prompt":"I need you to edit a Kotlin test file at `/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-cd563cee-8656-45be-b00b-25baabcba43c/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`.\n\nAdd four new test methods to the ShipmentControllerTest class. Add them at the end of the class, before the closing brace. Each test should follow the same pattern and style as the existing tests.\n\n**Test 1: Confirming a CREATED shipment changes its status to CONFIRMED**\n- Create a shipment with ID \"S-confirm-1\"\n- Confirm it via POST to `/shipments/S-confirm-1/confirm`\n- Assert response status is 200 OK\n- Assert the returned shipment has status \"CONFIRMED\"\n\n**Test 2: Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds (idempotent)**\n- Create a shipment with ID \"S-confirm-2\" (starts in CREATED)\n- Confirm it via POST to `/shipments/S-confirm-2/confirm`\n- Confirm it again via POST to `/shipments/S-confirm-2/confirm`\n- Assert the second confirmation also returns 200 OK\n- Assert the shipment still has status \"CONFIRMED\"\n\n**Test 3: Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns HTTP 409**\n- Directly save a CANCELLED shipment to the repository (use repository.save() with ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED)\n- Confirm it via POST to `/shipments/S-cancel/confirm`\n- Assert response status is 409 Conflict (use .andExpect(status().isConflict))\n- Assert jsonPath \"$.error.code\" equals \"SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION\"\n\n**Test 4: Confirming a non-existent shipment returns HTTP 404**\n- Confirm a non-existent shipment via POST to `/shipments/S-nonexistent/confirm`\n- Assert response status is 404 Not Found (use .andExpect(status().isNotFound))\n- Assert jsonPath \"$.error.code\" equals \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\"\n\nUse the MockMvc POST request builder pattern like the existing create test does. Use `.content()` when needed for the POST body.\n\nDo NOT modify existing tests. Only add the four new test methods.\n\nAfter editing, verify all four test methods are present and correctly formatted.","run_in_background":false},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17430,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011Y5ZWfvAjNan51P3wABDEq","session_id":"24402fd9-b714-4b41-86f7-6f1d1b0b434b","uuid":"b3667d6a-353b-42e5-9753-77d7ff502546","timestamp":"2026-09-11T20:48:36.434Z","request_id":"req_011CexJuirDdAt5yxYjHxf3h","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Implement the confirm shipment endpoint"}
